We are looking for a Software Engineer within Axon Product Development to help us build new functionality and add improvements to our SaaS platform. If you have an eye for writing code and are interested in agile methodologies, we’d like to meet you!


Key About Your Role
As a Software Engineer within a Scrum team, you use high\-quality code to solve complex puzzles. You collaborate with business analysts and test engineers to create new functionality for our customers and add internal improvements to our software. Together with the other members of your Scrum team, you take full responsibility for a vital part of the software.


You strive to deliver solid solutions by optimising their performance, usability, testability and maintainability and are proud of the products that you create. You analyse complex problems by actively cooperating with colleagues from various teams and find the best solution by combining different insights.


We also embrace AI\-assisted software engineering as part of our development lifecycle. Our engineers use tools such as Claude, ChatGPT and Codex to support activities across the SDLC. From exploring requirements and solution options, to writing and refactoring code, creating tests, debugging, documentation and code review. AI is a development aid, not a substitute for engineering judgement: you are expected to understand the solutions you deliver, validate AI\-generated output and remain accountable for its correctness, security, performance and maintainability.


As part of a large community of fellow software engineers, you are always looking for opportunities to improve your engineering skills, experiment with better ways of working and continuously improve our software and code base.


Key About Your Team
The Axon Product Development department consists of more than 120 colleagues, organised across 9 functional clusters (like Claims, Contracts, Financials, Request) and 16 Scrum teams. Together, they extend Axon’s functionality and continuously improve the product, ensuring it evolves in line with the changing needs of insurance companies and continues to deliver lasting value to our customers and their policyholders.


Check out our blog posts and videos to see what it is like to work at Keylane.


**About Keylane Property \& Casualty**
As the leading European supplier of robust, highly configurable and customer\-centric SaaS platforms to the insurance industry, Keylane offers solutions that optimise today’s business processes, unburdens our clients and empowers them to be future\-fit and agile.


With Axon, we aim to foster trust and empower lasting partnerships by providing an all\-in\-one SaaS platform that ensures a 24/7 uptime for our customers. We provide and implement continuous upgrades at no additional costs, guaranteeing that our customers are able to comply with the latest rules and regulations. Coupled with our commitment to backwards compatibility, we are a partner our clients can rely on with a platform that always delivers.

 **Requirements**  

* You are passionate about software engineering. You love to put your strong analytical skills to the test whilst working closely together with your team.
* You have experience with large technical ecosystems using Java, IntelliJ, Git, Gradle, Angular and Docker;
* You have experience working with SQL and databases (DB2, PostgreSQL);
* You are used to creating and performing unit, system and integration tests as part of your development work;
* You understand the Agile way of working, tools and techniques;
* You have an eye for writing code with attention to performance, scalability, maintainability and testability;

**Using AI**

* You are interested in using AI\-assisted development tools such as Claude, ChatGPT or Codex as part of the software development lifecycle. For example, to explore solutions, understand unfamiliar code, generate or improve code and tests, refactoring, troubleshoot issues, document solutions and support code reviews;
* You understand that AI\-generated code and suggestions must be critically evaluated, tested and reviewed. You take ownership of the quality, security, correctness and maintainability of the code you deliver;
* It’s a plus if you have experience with or interest in CI/CD (TeamCity, Bash, Puppet, Ansible, SaltStack, Chef, etc.) and in integrating AI\-assisted development into these practices.

* *A Certificate of Conduct (VOG) and reference check are part of the application process.*
* *Each employee within Keylane must follow training on information security and irrespective to the role basic information security responsibilities apply*

 **Benefits**  

* Starting with a monthly gross salary for a junior candidate between €3,500 and € 5,200 (medior) and between €4,300 and € 6,200 (senior) based on 40 hours per week;
* 8% holiday allowance of your total gross salary;
* A profit share;
* A pension scheme, with the option to save extra;
* Travel reimbursement: Receive a mileage allowance of €0\.23 per km or an NS Business Card, which can also be used for personal travel;
* 24 holiday days (with the option to buy extra) and 7 inclusion days, which can be exchanged with fixed Dutch national holidays, allowing you to take them when you like;
* Flexibility in working environment. As part of a hybrid working team, you will work partly from home and partly from the office. If you work in the office, a free lunch is waiting for you every day. If you work from home, you will receive a working from home allowance (€ 4 net per day) and internet allowance (€ 35 net per month);
* The possibility of working remotely from abroad for up to 2 months per year;
* The possibility to lease a bike through our bike leasing program;
* A one\-year contract that, subject to satisfactory performance, will be converted into a permanent contract;
* The opportunity to develop yourself at our Academy through courses and training, both professionally and personally;
* A comprehensive vitality offer to help you stay healthy. Read more here;
* An active and fun community of ‘Keylaners’. We also have after work drinks at our in\-house pub every Thursday.

Wil jij technische projecten tot leven brengen? Niet alleen achter een scherm werken, maar ook zien hoe jouw technische uitwerking daadwerkelijk wordt gerealiseerd? Dan voel jij je waarschijnlijk thuis in deze rol.


Als Project Engineer speel je een centrale rol in het realiseren van projecten. Zodra een project definitief wordt, zorg jij ervoor dat plannen, ontwerpen en klantwensen worden vertaald naar een technisch uitvoerbare oplossing. Je kijkt verder dan de tekening alleen. Je overziet het geheel, denkt vooruit en zorgt ervoor dat projecten technisch goed voorbereid de uitvoering ingaan.


Daarmee vorm je de verbindende schakel tussen engineering, projectleiding, uitvoering en klant. Je zorgt ervoor dat technische keuzes niet alleen op papier kloppen, maar ook in de praktijk uitvoerbaar zijn.


**Wat ga je doen?**


Vanaf het moment dat een project wordt overgedragen, neem jij de technische uitwerking onder je hoede. Je beoordeelt projectinformatie op volledigheid en uitvoerbaarheid, werkt technische oplossingen verder uit en zorgt ervoor dat alle betrokkenen beschikken over de juiste informatie.


Je houdt je onder andere bezig met:


* het technisch uitwerken van projecten naar werktekeningen;
* het opstellen en beheren van materiaallijsten;
* het beoordelen van technische haalbaarheid en uitvoerbaarheid;
* het afstemmen van technische vraagstukken met projectleiding, uitvoering en klanten;
* het verwerken van wijzigingen gedurende projecten;
* het signaleren van ontbrekende, onduidelijke of tegenstrijdige informatie;
* het bewaken van de samenhang tussen tekeningen, materialen en technische uitgangspunten;
* het meedenken over slimme, praktische en maakbare oplossingen.

Aan het einde van jouw voorbereiding is voor iedereen duidelijk wat er gerealiseerd moet worden, hoe dit uitgevoerd wordt en welke materialen daarvoor nodig zijn.


**Wat deze functie uniek maakt**




Je werkt aan projecten die daadwerkelijk gerealiseerd worden en ziet jouw werk terug in de praktijk. Tegelijkertijd krijg je veel ruimte om mee te denken over hoe processen slimmer, efficiënter en toekomstbestendiger kunnen worden ingericht.


De afdeling is volop in ontwikkeling. Dat betekent dat er ruimte is voor nieuwe ideeën, verbeteringen en innovaties. Of het nu gaat om standaardisatie, digitalisering of het slimmer inzetten van nieuwe technologieën, jouw bijdrage kan direct het verschil maken.


**Hier herken jij jezelf in**


Jij krijgt energie van technische vraagstukken en vindt het leuk om overzicht te houden binnen verschillende projecten. Je denkt vooruit, durft kritisch te zijn en zoekt altijd naar de beste oplossing.


Daarnaast neem je mee:


* mbo 4 of hbo werk\- en denkniveau;
* een technische achtergrond, bijvoorbeeld richting installatietechniek, werktuigbouwkunde of vergelijkbaar;
* kennis van AutoCAD is een pre;
* een sterk ontwikkeld technisch en ruimtelijk inzicht;
* een gestructureerde en nauwkeurige manier van werken;

**Wat kun je verwachten?**


Je komt terecht in een omgeving waar techniek, samenwerking en vakmanschap centraal staan. Je werkt samen met collega's die net als jij graag vooruitdenken en kwaliteit belangrijk vinden.


Daarnaast bieden we je:


* een uitdagende functie met veel afwisseling;
* ruimte om mee te bouwen aan processen en verbeteringen;
* een bruto maandsalaris van € 3\.500 tot € 4\.000 conform de cao Technische Groothandel.;
* 25 vakantiedagen en 12 Atv\-dagen, in totaal 37 vrije dagen;
* een premievrije pensioenregeling;
* reiskostenvergoeding van € 0,25 per kilometer;
* uitzicht op een langdurige samenwerking.

Krijg jij energie van techniek, verantwoordelijkheid en projecten die je daadwerkelijk terugziet in de praktijk? Solliciteer dan snel en we maken graag kennis met je.

**General Information**


**Type of contract** Fixed\-term contract, which may be extended subject to individual performance and organisational needs


**Who can apply?** EU nationals


**Salary** E/F (bracket 1 \- step 1\) full time monthly net salary: €4,982 plus benefits, for further information see what we offer.


**Working time** Full time


**Place of work** Frankfurt am Main, Germany


**Closing date** 06\.10\.2026


**Your team**


You will be part of the Directorate General Information Systems. Our Directorate General provides innovative, flexible and secure IT solutions to enable ECB and Eurosystem/ESCB staff to carry out their daily tasks. In addition to running and maintaining more than 100 available services, it is also responsible for the ECB’s IT governance frameworks. Our Directorate General consists of approximately 350 professionals delivering secure, scalable and data\-driven IT solutions that support central banking, banking supervision and shared services across the European Central Bank (ECB) and the European System of Central Banks (ESCB).  

We are looking for Application Development Specialists to join the Directorate General Information Systems. As an IT Specialist, you will further develop the portfolio of products that we managed and work on major ECB initiatives such as the Digital Euro project, the Analytics and Data project and the Integrated Reporting Framework project. You will have the opportunity to contribute to the Common Data Management Programme, an ESCB/SSM project that will design a future\-proof solution for a state\-of\-the\-art data and analytics environment for the ESCB and the Single Supervisory Mechanism.  

The ECB is an inclusive employer, and we strive to reflect the diversity of the population we serve. We encourage you to apply irrespective of age, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity, race, religious beliefs, sexual orientation or other characteristics.
**Your role**


We are looking for IT Application Development Specialists for the following roles in the ECB’s Common Data Management Programme: Data Engineering, Software Engineering and Cloud Engineering. We are also looking for an IT Specialist to work on the ECB’s Digital Euro project.  

As an IT Application Development Specialist, you will play a key role in the design, development and delivery of IT services, contributing to innovative solutions that support ECB’s objectives.  

In these roles, and depending on your skills and assigned responsibilities, you will:* design, develop and enhance IT services within the Directorate General Information Systems;
* develop and implement automated tests, builds, deployments and continuous integration pipelines to improve quality assurance and streamline delivery;
* collaborate with product owners and business stakeholders to refine user stories and prioritise tasks according to business value;
* actively participate in Agile ceremonies (sprint planning, daily stand\-ups, reviews and retrospectives);
* work with experts in architecture, security, governance, cloud computing and data protection to ensure compliance and quality;
* contribute to product team activities, share insights and present results to stakeholders when required.


We actively support professional development for our staff. Besides learning opportunities such as training and mentoring, we encourage and support horizontal mobility after some years in the same position.  

You will be part of a multicultural team that strives for continuous innovation to make a positive impact on the lives of European citizens.
**Qualifications, experience and skills**


Essential:  

* a bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in computer science, STEM, economics, finance, statistics or another relevant field (see How you can join us on our website for details on degree equivalences);
* in addition to the above, at least two years’ professional experience (including traineeships) in developing, maintaining, supporting and integrating activities within complex IT systems, such as Agile software development (particularly Scrum) or other product development/management methodologies;
* practical experience in Agile software development (e.g. SAFe, Scrum, Kanban);
* excellent analytical, drafting and presentation skills, with the ability to explain complex topics to diverse audiences;
* an advanced command of English (C1\) and an intermediate (B1\) command of at least one other official language of the EU, according to the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages.


Desired for the IT Specialist role in the Digital Euro project:  

* experience in designing, developing and delivering distributed systems with demanding performance, security and reliability requirements utilising frameworks such as Spring Boot, Hibernate or Micronaut;
* experience in building scalable, secure and efficient RESTful APIs and microservices, including integration with databases (e.g. MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB) and third\-party services;
* experience in implementing and managing DevOps practices in cloud platforms, including CI/CD pipeline creation, Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using tools like Terraform and containerisation with Docker and Kubernetes;
* an ability to understand existing codebases and build effective solutions on top of code developed by others.


Desired for the Data Engineering profile in the Common Data Management Programme:  

* proficiency in big data frameworks (e.g. Apache Spark, Flink, Kafka);
* strong experience with development and architecture ETL/ELT/reverse ETL pipelines and data workflow orchestration tools (e.g. Apache Airflow);
* solid knowledge of data modelling, data warehousing and modern storage solutions (e.g. Apache Iceberg, Iceberg REST Catalog, Trino, Impala, Hive, object storage);
* a sound understanding of connecting to data (e.g. ADBC, Iceberg REST Catalog, traditional ODBC/JDBC);
* experience designing, building, securing and optimising data lakes, data warehouses and data lakehouses.


Desired for the Software Engineering profile in the Common Data Management Programme:  

* proficiency in multiple programming languages (e.g. Java, Python, JavaScript, Go, Rust);
* experience building complex applications using languages and frameworks such as Java, Spring, JavaScript/TypeScript, Angular, Python, FastAPI;
* experience with infrastructure\-as\-code (e.g. Terraform), ideally on sovereign EU cloud providers;
* a strong knowledge of SQL and NoSQL databases (e.g. document, key\-value, column\-family, graph).


Desired for the Cloud Engineering role in the Common Data Management Programme:  

* experience in architecting secure large\-scale cloud applications addressing the operational, security, reliability, performance, cost and sustainability dimensions;
* strong experience in cloud provider managed solutions, e.g. managed databases, managed function as a service, managed containers;
* proficiency in designing and deploying Kubernetes\-based applications.


You engage collaboratively with others. You pursue team goals and learn willingly from other people’s diverse perspectives. You signal any need for change by explaining it and proposing alternative solutions. You analyse complex information effectively and can evaluate different views to arrive at solutions. You know and anticipate stakeholder needs.  

You are motivated to contribute to the ECB’s mission, to serve the citizens of the EU as a member of a public institution and to work with colleagues from all over Europe.
You are motivated to be part of a team and to develop and use your skills and competencies to achieve the aims of this position.
**Further information**


Temporary appointments may be extended or made permanent subject to organisational needs and budgetary constraints. This may result in a staff member with a non\-convertible fixed\-term contract being offered a convertible contract in accordance with the ECB Conditions of Employment.  

For additional information on this specific vacancy, you can speak to the hiring manager, Antonio Morlupi, on \+49 172 8948660 between 09:00 and 10:00 on Monday, 21, Wednesday, 23, Monday, 28 or Wednesday, 30 September.  


**Application and selection process**


The recruitment process for this position will be conducted remotely. It will include a written exercise, a presentation and interviews.  

If you are not selected for this position but are still considered suitable, you will be placed on a reserve list (see step 4 of How we hire), from which you might be considered for similar positions within the ECB.  

Find out how to apply for a position at the ECB.  

Read more about how you can join us.

At **Ocean Infinity**, we're on a bold mission to subsea data using innovative technology.


Using cutting\-edge robotics, autonomous technology and world\-class software, we're transforming how complex operations are carried out at sea. Our uncrewed systems are making ocean exploration and operations **safer, smarter and more sustainable**, helping unlock the vast potential of our oceans while reducing environmental impact.


This isn't a vision for the future. **It's happening right now.**


As we continue to push the boundaries of innovation and redefine what's possible in the maritime industry, we're looking for exceptional talent to join our fast\-growing team.


Ocean Infinity is seeking a Senior Application Engineer supporting internally developed Software in a live production environment. This role reports directly to the Head of Technology Support as part of a larger team supporting an innovative and high spec Tech environment.

 **Requirements** **What you will do!**

* Up to 3rd line support, resolving incidents and requests with internally developed software products and following up with detailed root cause analysis;
* Providing structured feedback to the internal development teams, identifying issues and driving improvements through real‑world insights;
* Mentoring generalist IT team members and working as a key contributor, and participant, to initiatives reducing the number of incidents, average resolution time and other reliability metrics;
* Working closely as a liaison between development and support teams to monitor and support frequent software releases as they move from development into production;
* Managing tickets to ensure response and resolution SLA’s are met;
* Managing high priority tickets from inception to resolution, communicating with users Incident management
* Participate in 24x7 on\-call support process.

**What we look for!**

* Strong background in 2nd/3rd Line Engineering, with a focus on coaching, mentoring, and supporting junior team members.
* Experience working with internally developed Software in production environments and supporting development teams either as a developer, senior QA Engineer or DevOps role;
* Proficiency working in Linux\-based environments with Docker, containerised applications, and shell scripting using PowerShell and Bash.
* Experience working with programming languages and frameworks such as JavaScript, Typescript and React; Python and/or C\#;
* Working knowledge of observability tools such as Prometheus, Grafana or Kibana to diagnose issues and interrogate software products;
* Good understanding and experience of ticketing systems, such as ServiceNow, Zendesk and ServiceDesk Plus;
* A can\-do attitude with a willingness to solve problems even if occasionally they may be considered “out of scope” for the role;
* Excellent time management skills and ability to prioritise work in a fast\-paced environment;
* Effective verbal and written communication skills, to interpret requirements and present findings;
* Interested in others and strives to act in the best interests of the team.

**Nice to have! ✨**

* At least two years of experience supporting internally developed applications as a 2nd/3rd line engineer;
* At least five years of experience working with programming languages;
* Experience working within an ITSM tool, adhering to ITIL framework including Incident Management, Problem Management and Change Management.



**Benefits** *\*Salary: £55,000 Per Annum\**

At DAC.digital, we are constantly growing our business, and as part of that growth we are strengthening our partnership with a fast\-growing client specializing in cloud computing, digital infrastructure, and innovative data platform solutions, providing scalable and secure technologies that support modern enterprise workloads and enable organizations to build and operate cloud\-native applications and services.


**Key information:**
--------------------


**Salary:**

* 25 000 – 30 000 PLN net/month – pure B2B contract
* 22 000 – 26 000 PLN net/month – B2B contract (days off included)
**It is vital that you have:**
------------------------------


* extensive experience in Platform Engineering, DevOps, or Data Platform Engineering;
* hands\-on experience with Apache Airflow, Jupyter Notebooks / JupyterHub, and Kubernetes;
* strong Python skills, particularly for APIs and automation;
* practical experience with ArgoCD and Helm;
* proven experience in designing, operating, and troubleshooting production data and analytics platforms;
* strong problem\-solving skills and the ability to independently analyze and resolve complex platform challenges;
* a high degree of autonomy and a strong hands\-on approach;
* experience with development and operations of the tools and platforms you work with;
* availability for occasional business trips to Germany;
* fluent English (C1\).

**We will be more than happy if you have:**
-------------------------------------------


* Dremio (administration, operations, and development);
* experience with modern data platform and cloud environments;
